       ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <p>And therefore the <em>Chalah</em> is fitting for the Kohen (<em>ra'ui lakohen</em>), but it becomes impure immediately (<em>nitma miyad</em>) in the air of the land of the nations (<em>ba'avir eretz ha'amim</em>) — for there is the aspect of the languages of the nations, which is the aspect of the blemish of speech (<em>pegam hadibur</em>) — namely, the aspect of speech without <em>da'as</em> as mentioned — drawn from the blemish of the Tree of Knowledge as mentioned.</p>

