       שֶׁהוּא עַל-יְדֵי חִבּוּר חֲסָדִים וּגְבוּרוֹת כַּנַּ"ל
       ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <p>And this is the aspect of the dough that is kneaded (<em>niloshes</em>) from flour and water — for the flour, which is the essential food (<em>ikar hamazon</em>), is drawn from <em>gevuros</em> [severities] in the aspect of the table in the north (<em>shulchan batzafon</em>), the aspect of the <em>gevuros</em> of rains (<em>gevuros geshamim</em>). And the water is the aspect of the waters of <em>chasadim</em>. And when the water and the flour join together (<em>kshenisvabbrim yachad</em>) — then it becomes the aspect of <em>da'as</em>, which comes through the joining of <em>chasadim</em> and <em>gevuros</em> (<em>chibur chasadim u'gevuros</em>) as mentioned.</p>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════
       CLAUSE 17
       וַאֲזַי חַיָּב בְּחַלָּה שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת רֵאשִׁית דַּעַת וְכַנַּ"ל
       ══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <p>And then one is obligated in <em>Chalah</em> — which is the aspect of the beginning of <em>da'as</em> (<em>reishis da'as</em>) — as mentioned above.</p>

